ove the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 10% earns above the cost of capital of 7.9%, but the 2pp spread is short of the 7pp moat bar; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.59).","It converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 2.22x.","ROE of 14% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.5% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.5x net debt to EBITDA ($516.6M of cash against $2.8B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, with interest covered 4.3x.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.33)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 5.3% over 3 years, 13.9% over 5 years and 6.3% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 18%).","At current returns, reinvesting 32% of profits supports about 3.2% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 13.5% a year over five years.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 8%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 7.0% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 4.9%, and institutions hold 97%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 3 sales over the past year, net $1.2M sold.","Shareholder yield is a modest 1.6% (1.6% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 0.6% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 22,155 employees, each generates about $272K of revenue, 0.8x the Industrials median, and revenue has grown 8.7% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","The company is founder-led, which often keeps management aligned with long-term owners.","CEO pay is $2.7M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).",